# Interview Story (STAR Format)

## Situation

While deploying the Governance layer of the CloudHustler Commerce Platform, Terraform failed during the creation of AWS IAM Access Analyzer, preventing the governance stack from completing successfully.

## Task

My responsibility was to determine whether the failure originated from Terraform, the AWS provider, or AWS IAM permissions, and restore the deployment without introducing unnecessary infrastructure changes.

## Action

I first validated the Terraform configuration and confirmed the resource definition was correct. I then verified the AWS provider was functioning by confirming that other governance services, including CloudTrail, AWS Config, GuardDuty, and Security Hub, had deployed successfully. With Terraform and the provider ruled out, I reviewed the IAM permissions assigned to the deployment role and compared them against the permissions required by AWS IAM Access Analyzer. This identified missing permissions needed to create the analyzer. After updating the deployment role with the required permissions, I reran the deployment.

## Result

Terraform successfully created the Access Analyzer, the governance deployment completed successfully, and the platform gained continuous visibility into unintended public and cross-account resource access. The incident also reinforced the importance of validating IAM permissions early when integrating new AWS services into Infrastructure as Code deployments.
